Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Using enumerated constants", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7715898249940033`*^9, 
  3.771589849034603*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"da654425-b3ed-4bea-b9bd-\
31425ffee00e"],

Cell["\<\
In the work below, we will need to make use of a WavelengthPreset which is an \
enumerated constant. To use the presets we need to load the enumeration and \
then access the constants by the syntax Mathematica uses for accessing \
contexts.

We can find the needed information in the ZOS-API help system. The wavelength \
presets are in the system data for OpticStudio. Under the help system, we \
locate the SystemData Namespace. The full name of the namespace is given at \
the top of the entry as \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]ZOSAPI.SystemData.\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]
\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7715900030706043`*^9, 3.7715900514148045`*^9}, {
   3.771590082474805*^9, 3.771590149649205*^9}, {3.7715901979950056`*^9, 
   3.7715902223474054`*^9}, {3.771590277321406*^9, 3.771590288927606*^9}, {
